141 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 105 0 R
/T (Improvisation is one of the most powerful, honest and deep ways to express one's thoughts and emotions through music. Current Jazz education often sees improvisation as an organized set of theoretical rules with a specific grammar, syntax and semantics. As a result, many modern improvisers spend the majority of their time working on chord-scales, finger patterns, intricate transcriptions and empty virtuosismo.)
/E (Improvisation is one of the most powerful, honest and deep ways to express one's thoughts and emotions through music. Current Jazz education often sees improvisation as an organized set of theoretical rules with a specific grammar, syntax and semantics. As a result, many modern improvisers spend the majority of their time working on chord-scales, finger patterns, intricate transcriptions and empty virtuosismo.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
