161 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 108 0 R
/E (Carry a music notebook with you everywhere, in which you will notate every good musical idea you hear. For example, cool chords, interesting melodies, a harmonic progression, a crazy rhythmic pattern; after some time you will have an incredible list of great ideas.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
162 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 108 0 R
/E (When I was 16, I started asking every musician I knew - from friends to famous artists - for their favorite chord. I would ask them to write it on my notebook. Instead of autographs, I had hundreds of amazing unique chords. \(Chick Corea's and Oscar Peterson's are my favorites\). Nowadays, my notebook became a true dictionary of incredible chords. Every day when I'm practicing or arranging something, I collect some cool ideas from my dictionary. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
163 0 obj
<<
