176 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 110 0 R
/E (Choose different movies/tv shows, mute the audio and improvise the soundtracks. Try to change the meaning of a scene by changing the music behind. This is an exercise to practice your ability to express emotional material in your music.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
177 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 110 0 R
/E (My favorite exercise is to take a horror movie and try to transform it into a comedy by improvising the music. Or you can do the opposite, pick a comedy movie and transform it into a drama. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
178 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 110 0 R
/E (You will then notice the importance of developing vocabulary to express different types of emotions in your music. Simply using fancy chords or scales won't be enough. You need repertoire, different ideas, imagination and aesthetic intelligence.  )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
